None of my saved requests have the URL /v3/oauth/token content. So all those claims of "successful" writes were also saved with empty content, even though the responses said success.

Wait, I confirmed earlier my read of oauth-token showed:
```json
{
  "ref": "request:oauth-token",
  "content": {
    "method": "POST",
    "url": "/v3/oauth/token",
    "headers": {
      "Content-Type": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
    },
    "protocol": "rest"
  },
  ...
}
```

That was real! And subsequent reads showed empty. Could it be that the read on the SAME entity returned empty, but a separate query gave the right content? That's strange.

